WEBVTT

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:14.253
Hi, friends. Gani here. This is Our Classroom Charter.

00:00:14.253 --> 00:00:20.505
Sit tall in your chair. Feet flat on the floor.

00:00:20.505 --> 00:00:24.257
Hands resting on your desk. Shoulders soft.

00:00:24.257 --> 00:00:28.008
Take one slow breath with me… and let it go.

00:00:28.008 --> 00:00:36.762
Every class has a way it treats each other. Some of it is just habit. But a class can also choose it, on purpose, together.

00:00:36.762 --> 00:00:46.766
That choosing is called a charter — our agreement. Not rules handed down. Words we pick ourselves, for our room.

00:00:46.766 --> 00:00:58.021
I will not give you the words. They are not mine to give. Your class has its own words, and they are the right ones.

00:00:58.021 --> 00:01:03.023
I will give you three questions. The answers are your charter. Let me show you.

00:01:03.023 --> 00:01:14.277
Question one: what helps everyone here feel safe? Bodies safe. Hearts safe. Safe to try, and safe to make a mistake.

00:01:14.277 --> 00:01:25.532
Question two: what helps everyone here learn? What do ears need? What do voices need? What does a thinking room sound like?

00:01:25.532 --> 00:01:36.786
Every voice counts toward the answers — including the quiet ones. A drawing counts as a word. A gesture counts as a word.

00:01:36.786 --> 00:01:46.791
Your teacher writes down the words your class chooses — your words, in your room, on your paper.

00:01:46.791 --> 00:01:48.041
Say the words together when they are new. Hear how they sound in your own voices. That sound is the promise starting.

00:01:48.041 --> 00:01:59.296
Now the honest part: some days the agreement will be hard to keep. That is not the charter failing. That is the charter's job arriving.

00:01:59.296 --> 00:02:10.550
When someone forgets, the move is remind and repair. Remind each other of the words — gently. Repair what got bumped.

00:02:10.550 --> 00:02:19.304
The charter is never a list for punishment, and it is never a reason to shame anyone. It is a promise we return to.

00:02:19.304 --> 00:02:20.554
And the class can change its words, together, when it learns something new. A charter is alive. It grows with you.

00:02:20.554 --> 00:02:29.308
Our words. Our promise. We return to it.

00:02:29.308 --> 00:02:35.561
Shoulders soft. Let your body rest.

00:02:35.561 --> 00:02:40.563
Hands down. One more slow breath… and let it go.

00:02:40.563 --> 00:02:46.815
Eyes open. Look around your classroom.

00:02:46.815 --> 00:02:53.068
You're ready for what's next.
